WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:05.440
There are a whole bunch of Trumpists and even
some non from Republicans who are getting

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:12.259
hugely bamboozled about the job market. And
as a result, the state of the economy. So

00:00:12.259 --> 00:00:18.640
let's first talk about if you want to analyze
how an economy is doing. I've always said

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:22.810
you can't look at one thing. The stock market
is a popular thing to look at. If the stock

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:25.820
market's up, we've got a good economy. If
it's down, we've got a bad economy, but it's

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:30.640
only one piece. It only affects on average
the wealthier who disproportionately owned

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:36.270
shares of stock. So by itself it doesn't tell
us how the economy is doing at all. The unemployment

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:40.910
rate is another piece, but the one that's
widely published, which is called the U three

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:45.040
you don't have to understand too much about
this, but when we hear about, Oh, unemployment

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:50.580
is 3.7% that's what's called the [inaudible].
It falls very short of telling us everything

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.080
that we need to know.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.790
Inflation and the consumer price index is
another element of how an economy is doing.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:01:03.710
The strength of the dollar affects other aspects
of our economy, the quality of the jobs that

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:12.110
people have, wage growth versus wage contraction
or wage stagnation. And very often this becomes

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:19.500
completely politicized. And in the end, any
casual observer of politics and economics

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:24.600
loses what it actually is that is taking place.
You have Republicans saying Republican presidents

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.320
have great job markets and economies, democratic
presidents have bad ones. The opposite true

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:34.010
for Democrats. And what I've been trying to
do is to get past that. So for example, I

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:39.380
told you during the 2012 presidential campaign,
whether Obama wins reelection or whether Mitt

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:46.760
Romney wins, the economy will likely be pretty
good the next four years. Republican labor

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:53.130
force conspiracy theories were wrong under
Barack Obama, but their labor force bragging

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:55.280
under Trump is also wrong.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:00.500
It's wrong on both sides of the equation as
the case may be. So the point today is that

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:07.020
one big piece that's missing from the great
job market that Donald Trump claims is the

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:14.959
quality of jobs. There is now a metric for
this, which is the Cornell CPA, U S private

00:02:14.959 --> 00:02:19.879
sector job quality index. And the name isn't
so much important, but what it does is it

00:02:19.879 --> 00:02:27.060
looks at the ratio of high wage, high hours
jobs to low wage, low hours jobs. There's

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:32.779
two ways that a job could be a low quality
job. It could be a low wage job or it could

00:02:32.779 --> 00:02:41.751
be a low hours job. This index has steadily
fallen since 1990 for the last 30 years. Part

00:02:41.751 --> 00:02:48.040
of this is because of the replacement of lots
of jobs that have been lost, making things

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:53.870
with service jobs. That includes restaurants
and many others. A whole bunch of the recent

00:02:53.870 --> 00:03:00.189
job gains, not just under the Trump administration,
but under Obama as well, have been in retail,

00:03:00.189 --> 00:03:02.290
leisure, hospitality.

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:08.499
That includes restaurants and other parts
of industry. Waste management is another area.

00:03:08.499 --> 00:03:15.230
The sectors that have been growing pay a far
lower weekly income than this job. The manufacturing

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:19.400
jobs and other jobs that have been going away
either because they've been eliminated or

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:25.200
moved overseas. So the top line U three rate,
that unemployment rate that's often publicize

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:31.109
the one Trump brags about that's under 4%
is low. Donald Trump, of course, when it was

00:03:31.109 --> 00:03:36.230
low under Obama, said the numbers were phony.
Now he brags about those numbers as evidence

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:40.950
of a great job market. But the more important
thing is that the quality of the jobs keeps

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:46.419
getting worse and because the income levels
of the high quality jobs keep going up while

00:03:46.419 --> 00:03:53.200
low quality jobs don't, this is furthering
inequality. The gap is growing even more in

00:03:53.200 --> 00:04:00.109
the United States. Now it's important to also
note very often the argument is made that

00:04:00.109 --> 00:04:05.459
when you have a low U three unemployment rate,
you have a lot of people working two jobs

00:04:05.459 --> 00:04:08.980
and that's a sign that that actually the economy
is weak.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:13.159
This is very often a red herring and it's
a red herring here. If you actually look at

00:04:13.159 --> 00:04:17.561
the number of people working two jobs right
now, it's quite low historically. So I, I

00:04:17.561 --> 00:04:22.139
don't, you know, I, I know that that's a talking
point I could use if I merely wanted to play

00:04:22.139 --> 00:04:26.020
partisan politics. That's not what I'm here
to do. I'm actually to tell you what the truth

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:31.150
is in the real world. The right loves using
that talking point, let's not use it. Okay?

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:35.729
We don't need to. This is where we come back
to our strategy from the left, from the side

00:04:35.729 --> 00:04:41.070
that wants the socially democratic reforms.
We can't pretend that a pretty good economy

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:47.530
isn't pretty good by the standards that are
used to measure economies. The economy is

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:53.190
pretty good right now. A lot of it has nothing
to do with Donald Trump whatsoever, but let's

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:56.319
focus on the things that aren't going well.

00:04:56.319 --> 00:05:03.120
People are working jobs that they hate to
keep healthcare. That's terrible. Okay. Wage

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:09.259
stagnation, really bad inequality, terrible
and furthered by what we're talking about

00:05:09.259 --> 00:05:15.240
here are the replacement of quality jobs with
low quality jobs. Um, lack of democratic workplaces.

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:20.500
We've talked about the democratization of
the workplace. That's a problem. Stock market

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:24.750
to the extent that it benefits some people,
it's riding high. It's not going to last forever.

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:31.050
It never does. We lose credibility when we
attack them in the factually indefensible

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:36.470
ways that they attack us. But we don't need
to do that because there is plenty of bad

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:41.620
to go around and that's where we should be
focusing our energies and to be, to be perfectly

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:50.040
Frank, it favors the policies we're advocating
for separating healthcare from employment,

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:54.990
democratizing the workplace, dealing with
inequality, whether it's with a higher progressive

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:58.110
marginal tax rate, taxing capital gains at
ordinary income.

00:05:58.110 --> 00:06:03.039
We have all the different tools in our, at
our disposal, all of the problems that are

00:06:03.039 --> 00:06:10.250
really the problems now point to the reforms
we want to make. So let's not maybe miss the

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:15.889
forest for the trees is not the right metaphor
here, but let's not do what they do when we

00:06:15.889 --> 00:06:20.880
don't need to do it. From a moral perspective,
let's not stoop to their level, but it also

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:26.069
doesn't benefit us because focusing on the
real problems points to the solutions being

00:06:26.069 --> 00:08:00.319
the suggestions we've been making social Democrats
have been making for

00:08:00.319 --> 00:08:09.220
a very long time.

